# NewUnera Consumer Nav — Canonical Implementation

## Enforcement

All `NewUnera/*.html` consumer pages MUST contain the exact `nav.nav` structure defined in this rule. The canonical live reference is `NewUnera/account-settings.html`. When adding or replacing a nav on any page — new or existing — copy the markup, CSS, and JS exactly as specified here. Never leave a simplified, legacy, or custom nav on any page.

**Target appearance:**
- Deep-blue sticky bar (`#173d47`), 44px tall, full-width, `z-index: 10001`
- Left: UNERA logo → DASHBOARD · WALLET · TRANSACT ▾ · CENTRES
- Right: notification bell (yellow badge) → pill-shaped wallet display: `[JS 🦊] [0x742d...3a8f ▾] [Polygon ▾]`
- Three interactive triggers: user avatar (user dropdown), wallet address (also opens user dropdown), network badge (network switcher)
- Mobile ≤480px: avatar-only circle + hamburger; all dropdowns become full-width fixed sheets

---

## Section 1 — Required `<head>` and `<body>` Setup

Every page must have in `<head>`:
```html
<html lang="en">
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
```

`<body>` must declare the active nav item:
```html
<body data-nav-active="dashboard">
```

Active values per page:

| Page | `data-nav-active` |
|---|---|
| `dashboard-enhanced.html` | `dashboard` |
| `wallet-enhanced.html` | `wallet` |
| `add-money.html`, `send-enhanced.html`, `stake.html`, `exchange.html` | `transact` |
| `explore-centres.html`, `centre-detail.html` | `centres` |
| All others (settings, KYC, notifications…) | omit or `""` |

Before `</body>`, after all inline scripts:
```html
<script src="consumer-app-nav.js"></script>
```

After the page's inline `<style>` block, include the shared nav stylesheet:
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="consumer-app-nav.css">
```

Pages in subfolders must use the correct relative path (e.g. `../../consumer-app-nav.css` from `data-mapping/.../screens/`).

