### Mobile drawer accordion contract

Every consumer page with a hamburger drawer MUST:

1. Link [`NewUnera/consumer-app-nav.css`](NewUnera/consumer-app-nav.css) — accordion CSS lives there; do not rely on page-inline duplicates.
2. Keep `#mobileUserMenu` and `#mobileNotificationsSection` placeholders in the drawer HTML (Section 4).
3. Populate on load (automatic via [`consumer-app-nav.js`](NewUnera/consumer-app-nav.js) `hydrateUserMenus()` on `DOMContentLoaded`):
   - `#desktopMenuContainer` ← `renderUserMenu('desktop')` (includes My Profile, Account Settings, My Wallet, Dashboard, **Centres**)
   - `#mobileUserMenu` ← `renderUserMenu('mobile')` (same items in mobile accordion; **Centres** is below Dashboard — not in `ul.mobile-nav-links`)
   - `#mobileNotificationsSection` ← `renderNotificationPanel('mobile')` (page script, when notifications are implemented)
4. Collapse user accordion by default: `#mobileUserDropdown` has `max-height: 0` until `.open` is toggled via `toggleMobileUserDropdown()` (defined in [`consumer-app-nav.js`](NewUnera/consumer-app-nav.js)).
5. Notifications block uses the same accordion shell (`.mobile-notif-profile` + `#mobileNotificationDropdown`) toggled via `toggleMobileNotificationPanel()` (also in `consumer-app-nav.js`).
6. **Height caps (never 500px):** `#mobileUserMenu .mobile-user-dropdown.open` → `min(75dvh, 56rem)` (~896px) so NETWORK + ACCOUNT links are not clipped. `#mobileNotificationsSection .mobile-user-dropdown.open` → `min(45dvh, 24rem)` with internal scroll (hidden scrollbar).
7. **Mutual exclusion:** opening the user accordion closes the notifications accordion and vice versa.
8. **Drawer close:** `closeMobileDrawerAccordions()` in `consumer-app-nav.js` resets user, notifications, and TRANSACT accordions when `.mobile-menu` loses `.active` (MutationObserver).
9. **TRANSACT accordion:** Section label is a button with right chevron; sub-links live in `#mobileTransactSubmenu`. Toggle via `toggleMobileTransactAccordion()`; **expanded by default** whenever the drawer opens (`aria-expanded="true"`). Legacy flat markup (`li.mobile-nav-section-label` + sibling `mobile-nav-sub` rows) is upgraded on `DOMContentLoaded` by `initMobileTransactAccordion()` in `consumer-app-nav.js`.

**Failure modes:**
- Omitting `.mobile-user-dropdown { max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }` causes wallet/network/account links to render fully expanded as a floating panel outside the drawer flow.
- Using `max-height: 500px` on the user accordion causes `#mobileNotificationsSection` to overlap ACCOUNT links (My Profile, etc.) at the bottom of the panel.

