## Section 8 — Auth State Behavior

`consumer-app-nav.js:syncNavAuthState()` and `applyNavWalletSession()` read localStorage and toggle:

| Condition | Nav shows |
|---|---|
| Not logged in | `#navAuthLinks` (LOG IN / SIGN UP); hides bell, wallet pill |
| Logged in, wallet NOT connected | `#navConnectBtn`; **avatar-only** `#navWalletDisplay` (`data-wallet-session="disconnected"`); bell visible; user dropdown with status chip + **Connect wallet** menu item |
| Logged in, wallet connected | `#walletNavLink`, full 3-part `#navWalletDisplay` pill; hides CONNECT |

localStorage keys: `unera_user`, `isLoggedIn`, `loggedIn`, `walletConnected`, `walletAddress`, `walletBalance`, `selectedNetwork` (JSON `{id, label, color}`).

IDs updated by `syncNavAuthState`: `navUserInitials` / `.user-avatar-nav` (initials), `.user-name-nav` (name), `navWalletAddress`, `navWalletBalance`, `navNetworkLabel`, `drawerWalletAddress`, `drawerWalletBalance`, `drawerWalletNetwork`.

### Switch wallet / Connect modal (`openConnectModal`)

`consumer-app-nav.js` defines `window.switchWalletFromNav()` (closes user dropdown, calls `openConnectModal`) and `window.openConnectModal()` with this **fallback chain** (first match wins):

| Priority | Function / target | Pages |
|----------|-------------------|-------|
| 1 | `window.openWalletAuthModal({ intent: 'connect' })` | `index.html`, `login_2.html`, `signup_2.html` (when `shared/wallet-auth.js` loaded) |
| 2 | `window.showWalletSelectionModal()` | `account-settings.html` (dynamic provider grid modal) |
| 3 | `#connectModal` — add `.active`, reset DEV scenario to happy, lock body scroll | `dashboard-enhanced.html`, `wallet-enhanced.html`, etc. |

**Account Settings pin:** after `<script src="consumer-app-nav.js">`, assign `window.openConnectModal` to call `showWalletSelectionModal()` so Switch wallet always opens the *Connect. Contribute. Change lives.* modal (see `NewUnera/account-settings.html`).

**Do not** leave a page-level `openConnectModal` before `consumer-app-nav.js` without a post-nav override — the shared script loads last and owns the global.

