## Section 9 — What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never use `background: #FFFFFF` or `background: var(--primary-green)` on `.nav`
- ❌ Never omit `#notificationBellWrapper`, `#navWalletDisplay`, or `#userDropdown`
- ❌ Never omit `<script src="consumer-app-nav.js"></script>`
- ❌ Never ship `openConnectModal` as `openWalletAuthModal`-only — Switch wallet and CONNECT become no-ops on pages with `showWalletSelectionModal` or `#connectModal` only
- ❌ Never hardcode `#10B981`, `#0EA5E9`, or `#EC4899` in nav styles
- ❌ Never use `linear-gradient` on nav chrome
- ❌ Never use `../Brand Guide/Unera-Horizontal.png` — use `NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg`
- ❌ Never use `Unera Black Text Nav.svg` in the sticky nav — only in the mobile drawer header
- ❌ Never omit the `🦊` emoji on `.nav-wallet-metamask-badge` — intentional V2 exception
- ❌ Never set dropdown `z-index` lower than 10002
- ❌ Never leave `#navWalletDisplay` without `position: relative`
- ❌ Never leave a `<nav class="stablecoin-nav">` or any other non-canonical nav on a consumer page
- ❌ Never use `.nav-wallet-network-trigger` or runtime-merge address+network into one button — use separate `.nav-wallet-trigger` + `.nav-network-badge`
- ❌ Never put Wallet copy/switch/disconnect actions inside `#networkDropdown` — those belong in `#userDropdown` only
- ❌ Never use `.notification-panel { width: 360px }` as a single-class selector — the `.user-dropdown-nav` base rule (also single-class, declared later) overrides it to 280px. Always use the compound selector `.user-dropdown-nav.notification-panel { width: 360px }` so specificity (0,2,0) beats `.user-dropdown-nav` (0,1,0). Apply the same compound selector in `@media (max-width: 768px)` for the 320px override.
- ❌ Never omit `<link rel="stylesheet" href="consumer-app-nav.css">` on pages that populate `#mobileUserMenu` — mobile accordion CSS is delivered via that file.
- ❌ Never ship a mobile drawer without `.mobile-user-dropdown { max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }` — dropdown content leaks outside the drawer as a detached panel.
- ❌ Never use `max-height: 500px` on `#mobileUserMenu .mobile-user-dropdown.open` — ACCOUNT links overlap the Notifications header.

