## Section 10 — Migration Guide

**Signals of a legacy nav to replace:**
- White nav background or green/primary-green on `.nav`
- `.user-profile-nav` as a sibling of `#navWalletDisplay` (not nested inside it)
- `<nav class="stablecoin-nav">` element
- Missing `#notificationBellWrapper` or `#navWalletDisplay`
- `.nav-links` without `role="list"`

**Steps:**
1. Remove the entire `<nav>…</nav>` block and any `<!-- Mobile Menu -->` + overlay siblings
2. Paste the complete nav HTML from Section 4
3. Replace the nav CSS block (search `.nav {`) with Section 5 CSS
4. Replace nav JS toggle functions with Section 6 Block 1; add hamburger IIFE (Block 2)
5. Set `data-nav-active` on `<body>` per Section 1 table
6. Confirm `<script src="consumer-app-nav.js"></script>` is last script before `</body>`
7. Confirm `<link rel="stylesheet" href="consumer-app-nav.css">` is present after inline `<style>`
8. Verify `:root` includes all tokens from Section 3

