## Section 12 — Implementation Plan Quality Standard

When asked to **plan a nav migration** (new page, bulk migration, or any "duplicate the nav" request), the plan MUST meet this bar. A weak plan produces blank icons, wrong widths, and missing JS — every past failure in this project traces back to an under-specified plan.

### Mandatory plan sections

Every plan must include ALL of the following. Never omit or combine sections.

#### A. Scope table
List every file to create or edit. Mark files that must NOT be touched (e.g. backend files, shared JS).

| File | Action | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| `NewUnera/foo.html` | Edit | Nav CSS + HTML + JS replacement |

#### B. Exact `:root` token audit
Read the target file's `:root` block. List which tokens from Section 3 are **missing** and must be added. Quote the exact CSS lines to insert and the line number to insert after.

#### C. CSS replacement plan
- Quote the **exact opening comment** and selector of the old CSS block to be replaced (e.g. `/* Navigation */\n.nav {`)
- State the **exact opening comment and selector** of the replacement (Section 5 canonical CSS)
- List any **page-specific CSS** in the old block that must be preserved (stat cards, hero, table styles, etc.) — state the line range
- Explicitly call out the compound selector rule: `.user-dropdown-nav.notification-panel { width: 360px }` — never `.notification-panel { width: 360px }`
- Explicitly call out the responsive overrides: `@media (max-width: 768px)` must use `.user-dropdown-nav.notification-panel { width: 320px }` (same compound)

#### D. HTML replacement plan
- Quote the **exact opening tag** and **exact closing tag** (with line numbers) of the old `<nav>`, mobile overlay `<div class="mobile-menu-overlay">`, and mobile drawer `<div class="mobile-menu">` blocks
- List every legacy anti-pattern present (see Section 10) — e.g. "Has `.user-profile-nav` sibling — must be removed", "Mobile drawer uses `Unera White Text Nav.svg` — must change to `Unera Black Text Nav.svg`"
- Confirm `data-nav-active` value for this page (Section 1 table)

#### E. JavaScript replacement plan
- Identify the old `<script>` block that contains nav toggle functions (quote first and last line, with line numbers)
- State which page-specific functions in that block MUST be preserved (e.g. `filterByCategory`, `filterCentres`) — quote their signatures
- State that Block 1 (toggle functions) replaces the identified block
- State that Block 2 (hamburger IIFE) goes in a separate `<script>` immediately before `<script src="consumer-app-nav.js"></script>`
- State that `NOTIFICATION_ICONS` (Section 6 canonical constant, Material Symbols FILL=1 paths) replaces any existing `NOTIFICATION_ICONS` or `PANEL_ICON_PATHS` with Heroicons stroke paths

#### F. Notification item rendering audit
Check whether the target page has:
1. `NOTIFICATION_ICONS` constant — is it using **Heroicons stroke paths** (broken) or **Material Symbols FILL=1 paths** (correct)?
2. `renderNotificationItem` SVG wrapper — is it `viewBox="0 -960 960 960" fill="currentColor"` (correct) or `viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"` (broken with Material Symbols paths)?
3. Notification item CSS (`.notif-item`, `.notif-item-icon`, `.notif-type-*`) — present?

State the exact replacement for each issue found.

#### G. Post-migration verification steps (manual, in browser)
List exact click sequences:
1. Open page → confirm nav is `#173d47`, 44px tall
2. Click bell → confirm `#notificationPanel` is **360px wide** (open DevTools → Computed → width; must NOT be 280px)
3. Confirm notification icons are **filled glyphs**, not blank grey circles
4. Click avatar → confirm `#userDropdown` is 280px wide, right-aligned under `#navWalletDisplay` (not offset left under avatar), with header (name, email, wallet chip) and menu items
5. Click wallet address trigger → confirm `#userDropdown` opens; Switch wallet appears above Disconnect Wallet when connected
6. Click network badge → confirm `#networkDropdown` has MAINNET (Ethereum, Base) + TESTNET (Sepolia, Base Sepolia with badges); active has checkmark; pill is 3-part (not merged `address · network` button)
7. Resize to ≤480px → confirm hamburger appears, nav links hidden, wallet collapses to 36×36 circle
8. Open hamburger → confirm user profile accordion collapsed; tap header → network + account links expand inline

### What makes a plan fail (anti-patterns)

| Anti-pattern | Consequence |
|---|---|
| Missing `.mobile-user-dropdown { max-height: 0 }` | User/network/account panel leaks outside drawer |
| `max-height: 500px` on user accordion | ACCOUNT links hidden under Notifications header |
| Page populates `#mobileUserMenu` but omits `consumer-app-nav.css` | Same detached-panel bug on any new page |
| Uses `.notification-panel { width: 360px }` (single class) | Panel renders at 280px |
| `NOTIFICATION_ICONS` has `stroke-linecap` Heroicons paths | All icons are invisible (blank grey circles) |
| SVG wrapper uses `fill="none" stroke="currentColor"` with Material Symbols paths | Icons invisible (no stroke geometry in MS paths) |
| Plan says "align with Section 5" without quoting old selectors | Implementer replaces wrong CSS block |
| Plan omits notification item CSS block | Icons render with no background tint, no sizing |
| Block 2 hamburger IIFE placed inside Block 1 `<script>` | Mobile menu broken |
| Forgets to change mobile drawer logo to `Unera Black Text Nav.svg` | White-on-white logo in mobile drawer |
| Omits `position: relative` on `#navWalletDisplay` | Wallet dropdowns position incorrectly |
